---
name: quality-review
description: Review the changes for how well the code adheres to the repo's documented code quality standards. This is intended to be used only after the code is in a functional state. Use when the user asks specifically for a code quality review. Runs review in a sub-agent.
---

The goal is to review the current changes for code quality. Your job is basically to defend the codebase against creeping complexity, debt, and bloat.

Make sure you understand what the reference point is. Typically it's the current HEAD. But it could also be a specific commit or branch. In some cases the user might ask for a review of the entire codebase. Read the changes carefully, as well as unchanged code that they interact with. Make sure you understand what's going on, and why the changes are being made. Ask for clarification if things are unclear.

The coding standards are in `CODING_STANDARDS.md`. The document outlines the general architecture, and provides a list of concrete code smells to review for. Write a report flagging the lines where you think a rule is being bent/broken. For each issue, cite the rule and give a short justification and recommended path to fix. 1-3 sentences per issue. Use a numbered list so we can refer back to the issues.

Many issues will be judgement calls. Mark the issues with high, medium, low confidence. False positives are preferred to false negatives. We will filter the list to decide which should be fixed. But we should still aim for precision > 0.25.
